    icon: '🃏',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. **Draw**: Take from stock or pick up the entire discard pile (if the top card is immediately melded). 2. **Meld**: Place sets (same rank) or runs (same suit sequence) on the table. 3. **Discard**: End turn by placing one card face up on the pile. 4. **Pot**: The first player to empty their hand takes the first 'pot' hand. 5. **End**: Round ends when a player with at least one biriba empties their hand again.",
    Player: "1. **Draw**: Take from stock or pick up the entire discard pile (if the top card is immediately melded). 2. **Meld**: Place sets (same rank) or runs (same suit sequence) on the table. 3. **Discard**: End turn by placing one card face up on the pile. 4. **Pot**: The first player to empty their hand takes the first 'pot' hand. 5. **End**: Round ends when a player with at least one biriba empties their hand again.",
    objective: "Score points through melds and go out. You must complete at least one 'biriba' (meld of 7+ cards) to be eligible to go out.",
    gameplay: "1. **Draw**: Take from stock or pick up the entire discard pile (if the top card is immediately melded). 2. **Meld**: Place sets (same rank) or runs (same suit sequence) on the table. 3. **Discard**: End turn by placing one card face up on the pile. 4. **Pot**: The first player to empty their hand takes the first 'pot' hand. 5. **End**: Round ends when a player with at least one biriba empties their hand again.",
    keyRules: [
      'Jokers and 2s are wild cards.',
      'Clean Biriba (no wilds) = 500 pts. Dirty Biriba (with wilds) = 300 pts.',
      'Going out awards 100 points.',
      'Cards left in hand are negative points.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '4 players in two fixed partnerships (North-South vs East-West).',
      deck: '108 cards: Two standard 52-card decks plus four Jokers. Jokers and 2s are wild.',
      equipment: 'Standard pack with jokers, score pad.',
      dealing: "Deal 11 cards to each player. Two 'pots' (reserve hands) of 11 cards each are placed face down. Remaining cards form the stock.",
    },
    turnFlow: "1. **Draw**: Take from stock or pick up the entire discard pile (if the top card is immediately melded). 2. **Meld**: Place sets (same rank) or runs (same suit sequence) on the table. 3. **Discard**: End turn by placing one card face up on the pile. 4. **Pot**: The first player to empty their hand takes the first 'pot' hand. 5. **End**: Round ends when a player with at least one biriba empties their hand again.",
    moveValidityConditions: {
      ante: 'Biriba is a point-based partnership rummy game and does not utilize a monetary or chip-based ante system.',
      deal: 'The initial distribution of cards and creation of reserve pots is performed automatically by the system dealer.',
      reveal_market: 'The stock remains face down; the only public cards are those in the discard pile or on the table tableau.',
      buy_market: 'Cards cannot be purchased; they are drawn from the stock or captured from the discard pile for free.',
      buy_stock: 'Drawing from the stock is a standard mandatory turn action and does not involve a purchase cost.',
      fold: 'Partnerships must participate until one player empties their hand after fulfilling the biriba requirement.',
      check: 'The game uses a draw-and-meld structure rather than a vying structure where checking would be an option.',
      call: 'There is no pot or bet to match in Biriba; competition is based on point accumulation and shedding.',
      bet: 'Success is determined by total point accumulation on a scorecard rather than through wagering of assets.',
      raise: 'There are no wagering rounds in Biriba, so the value of the hand cannot be increased via raises.',
      declare: "Must hold the required cards during the player's turn.",
      reveal_hand: 'Hands remain private until cards are played onto the table; no separate reveal phase occurs.',
      award_pot: 'Winning points are added to a cumulative session total rather than awarded from a physical pot.',
      play_card: 'Cards are melded or discarded rather than played to tricks; melds are permanent until the round ends.',
      draw: 'Start of turn action.',
      discard: 'Mandatory to end the turn.',
      pass: 'Players must draw and discard every turn; passing a turn without action is not permitted.',
      bid: 'Standard Biriba does not use a bidding system; the game objectives are fixed by rule.',
      meld: 'Minimum 3 cards; must include natural cards.',
      go_out: 'Requires at least one biriba to have been melded by the team.',
    },
    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 11 card(s) per player.',
      "Rule example: Score points through melds and go out. You must complete at least one 'biriba' (meld of 7+ cards) to be eligible to go out.",
      "Turn-flow example: 1. **Draw**: Take from stock or pick up the entire discard pile (if the top card is immediately melded). 2. **Meld**: Place sets (same rank) or runs (same suit sequence) on the table. 3. **Discard**: End turn by placing one card face up on the pile. 4. **Pot**: The first player to empty their hand takes the first 'pot' hand. 5. **End**: Round ends when a player with at least one biriba empties their hand again.",
      'Scoring example: Clean biriba = 500, Dirty biriba = 300, Going out = 100. Card values: Joker 20, 2s 10, Aces 15, 8-K 10, 3-7 5, matching the standard Pagat rules. Cards left in hand are subtracted. First team to reach target score (typically 2,500 or 5,000 points)..',
